*20
/           QUESTIONS:
/1.  THE ADJECTIVES USED TO DESCRIBE "THE EYE" IN THE
/ARTICLE ARE
/(A) BLACK, VERY DANGEROUS
/(B) WINDY, STRANGE
/(C) WEIRDEST, MOST AWESOME
/(D) POWERFUL, TERRIFYING
	C
/2.  THE SHAPE OF "THE EYE" IS
/(A) CIRCULAR
/(B) CYLINDRICAL
/(C) ELIPTICAL
/(D) CONICAL
	A
/3.  "THE EYE" IS BOUNDED BY
/(A) A BLACK CIRCULAR BAND
/(B) HORIZONTAL BLACK BANDS
/(C) HEAVY ORANGE LINES
/(D) A VERTICAL CURTAIN OF BLACK
	D
/4.  THE DIAMETER OF "THE EYE" IS
/(A) APPROXIMATELY 1 MILE
/(B) APPROXIMATELY 5 MILES
/(C) APPROXIMATELY 6 MILES
/(D) 10 TO 15 MILES
	D
/5.  THE HURRICANE IS DRIVEN BY GALES
/(A) 180 TO 200 MPH
/(B) 40 TO 60 MPH
/(C) 400 TO 500 MPH
/(D) 10 TO 20 MPH
	A
/6.  "THE EYE" IS
/(A) FURIOUSLY ACTIVE
/(B) DRENCHED WITH RAINS
/(C) SOMETIMES CALM ENOUGH SO THAT BIRDS OR SHIPS CAN
/   TAKE REFUGE IN IT
/(D) COLD AND SNOWY
	C
/7.  "THE EYE"
/(A) HAS NO MOTION
/(B) MOVES AROUND IN CIRCLES
/(C) MOVES FORWARD AT ABOUT 100 MPH
/(D) MAY MOVE FORWARD WITH A MOTION OF ONLY 10 TO 15 MPH
	D
/8.  AS THE SEARCH PLANE CRUISES AROUND "THE EYE" IT
/(A) FLIES THROUGH IT AND REPORTS ITS LOCATION
/(B) FLIES INTO IT AND STAYS THERE
/(C) AVOIDS IT
/(D) PUTS THE DROPSONDE INTO ACTION
	D
/9.  THE FUNCTIONS OF THE DROPSONDE ARE TO
/(A) RECORD THE DIRECTION AND VELOCITY OF THE WIND
/(B) RECORD THE DIAMETER AND HEIGHT OF "THE EYE"
/(C) RECORD THE ATMOSPHERIC PRESSURE, TEMPERATURE, AND
/      HUMIDITY
/(D) RECORD THE SIZE OF THE AREA WHICH THE HURRICANE IS
/      COVERING
	C
/10.  WHEN FUEL GETS LOW THE SEARCH PLANE LEAVES "THE EYE"
/ON THE WESTERN SIDE BECAUSE
/(A) THE PLANE IS FACING THE SUN
/(B) THE HURRICANE IS STRONGEST IN THE WEST
/(C) "THE EYE" IS IN THE WESTERN PART OF THE HURRICANE
/(D) EXPERIENCE HAS TAUGHT HIM A HEARTY TAILWIND CAN BE
/    PICKED UP THERE
	D
